"This exception matters because it completes a pattern this unit's lessons on the seven emotions have built up piece by piece: every one of the emotions, including the one usually treated as harmless, is capable of disrupting qi if it's extreme enough, sudden enough, or sustained long enough. Chinese medicine doesn't sort emotions into a permanently safe half and a permanently risky half; it sorts extremity itself as the actual variable that matters, regardless of which of the seven emotions happens to be involved.": "7c52bb876cec",
